BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:João Ruas: Osso
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T200000
DTSTAMP:20261106T110227Z
UID:dothebay-18019940@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Arts & Family
DESCRIPTION:Brazilian artist João Ruas began his “OSSO” series during
  the lockdowns of 2020\, as a way of creating something that would allow h
 im to escape reality\, and that could be produced more quickly than painti
 ngs. The ongoing realities of today continue to lend themself to escapism\
 , which is why\, six years on\, Ruas continues producing this series. The 
 process follows two rules: the same materials are used\, just graphite and
  paper\, and the drawings have the same dimensions. Reflecting back\, Ruas
  believes that Goya’s “Caprichos” and Jean Giraud’s “Forty Days 
 in the Desert\,” two series he greatly admires\, may have had some influ
 ence during the conception.\n\nThis chosen technique\, pencil\, is Ruas’
 s favorite way of expressing the ideas and scenarios that make up his inte
 rnal mythology\, a concept he has been developing for years. A human amalg
 am that seeks to unite the most disparate traditions and artistic expressi
 ons separated by geography and time itself.\n\nThis exhibition features 19
  works\, although the series already comprises more than 50 completed draw
 ings.\n\nFree\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/5/joao-ruas-
 osso-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.788704;-122.4138
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35238364/8730e882-3ebc-485a-8cfc-fd576fce4f64.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261106T110227Z
LOCATION:Ryan Graff Contemporary\, 804 Sutter Street\, San Francisco\, CA\
 , 94109
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/5/joao-ruas-osso-tickets
END:VEVENT
