DESCRIPTION:Doc Shorts features five compelling documentaries that reveal 
 how dance carries memory\, identity\, and cultural legacy across the globe
 . From a martial art form kept alive by one woman in rural Bangladesh to a
  near-forgotten ritual dance revived by a new generation in Colombia\, sev
 eral of these films capture communities working to ensure their traditions
  aren’t lost to time. For those drawn to the stories behind the movement
 \, these real-life portraits are tender and resonant.\n\nPublished by Danc
 ers' Group\nContains information from CalDiscovery (caldiscovery.com)\, OD
 bL 1.0\n\nDetails: https://dancersgroup.org/calendar/doc-shorts-2026-sf-da
 nce-film-festival/?utm_source=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san
