CATEGORIES:Arts & Family
DESCRIPTION:Please join us at the Crissy Field Center on Presidio Tunnel T
 ops for a family-friendly Día de los Muertos & Diwali event in the park!\
 n\nObserved annually in the fall season\, these two distinct cultural cele
 brations come together in a national park to honor South Asian and Latinx 
 traditions. Designed intentionally as a celebration and a learning opportu
 nity\, attendees are invited to participate in a wide range of activities 
 that include arts and crafts\, storytelling\, cultural dance\, song\, and 
 a fire ceremony\, and learn about social and environmental justice issues 
 in both cultures.\n\nHosted by the Presidio Trust and Parks Conservancy wi
 th Alliance for South Asians Taking Action.\n\nSee the schedule below (ple
 ase note that some activities require additional registration):\n\n10-10:3
 0am: Ceremonial Opening & Welcome at the Field Station Plaza\n10:30-11:30a
 m: Cultural Art Sessions at Crissy Field Center (Note: There are multiple 
 time slots for art sessions)\n10:30am-12:30pm: Planting as Remembrance Qua
 rtermaster Reach (please register here)\n11:30am-12pm: Fire Ceremony at Cr
 issy Field Center\n12-12:30pm: Duniya Dance and Drum Company performance a
 t Presidio Steps/Field Station Plaza\n12:30-1:30pm: Cultural Art Sessions 
 at Crissy Field Center (Note: There are multiple time slots for art sessio
 ns)\n1:30-2pm: Fire Ceremony at Crissy Field Center\n2:30-3pm: Closing Per
 formance at Crissy Field Center Courtyard - Mexican guitar/vocal music per
 formance by Diana Gameros\n\nFree\nPresidio Trust\, Golden Gate Parks Cons
 ervancy & Alliance for South Asians Taking Action Present\n\nDetails: http
 s://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/7/dia-de-los-muertos-and-diwali-festival-t
 ickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/dia
 -de-los-muertos-diwali-festival-crissy-field-sf/
