CATEGORIES:Arts & Family
DESCRIPTION:Few and Far Women\, one of the world’s largest women’s art
  collective crews\, is proud to announce its monumental 15-year anniversar
 y celebration. Bringing together an extraordinary international lineup of 
 creators\, the collective is hosting an exclusive pop-up art show on Satur
 day\, November 7th\, 2026\, from 6:00 PM to Midnight at the renowned 111 M
 inna Gallery (located at 111 Minna St.\, San Francisco\, CA 94105). This m
 ilestone event is strictly 21+.\n\nOver the past decade and a half\, Few a
 nd Far Women has been making their mark worldwide\, championing the vital 
 importance of women in art and skateboarding. Remaining fiercely consisten
 t in their mission of "women refining the arts of the streets"\, members h
 ave crossed borders and cultures to break barriers\, reclaim public spaces
 \, and uplift female creators in historically male-dominated subcultures.\
 n\nIn addition to celebrating 15 years of creative resilience\, community 
 building\, and groundbreaking murals\, this special pop-up event will serv
 e as a launchpad to build support and generate financial backing to bring 
 our highly anticipated 15-year retrospective coffee table book to life. At
 tendees and supporters will have a unique opportunity to contribute to the
  realization of this upcoming publication\, which will permanently archive
  the global history\, artwork\, skateboarding culture\, and international 
 impact of the crew - whilst getting a first glimpse of this photographic\,
  and illustrated chronicle.\n\nWhat to expect: a multi-media co...\n\n111 
 Minna Gallery Presents:\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/7/
 a-15-year-celebration-of-few-and-far-women-an-art-and-skate-collective-pop
 -up-show-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funche
 ap.com/women-15year-art-celebration-skate-popup-111-minna/
