DESCRIPTION:David Yu via FlickrHonor the service and sacrifice of our Arme
 d Forces at San Francisco’s Annual Veterans’ Day Parade on Sunday\, No
 vember 8\, 2026.\nhe annual Veterans Day Parade will begin at 11 a.m. in t
 he Fisherman’s Wharf area of the northern waterfront. Parade formation w
 ill begin at 10 a.m. Streets will be closed and Muni will reroute around t
 he event.\nThe parade typically begins at 11 am at North Point between Pow
 ell and The Embarcadero.\n\n2026 Veterans’ Day Parade\nSunday\, November
  8\, 2026 | 11 am\nFisherman’s Wharf\, SF\nFREE\n2026 Details from San F
 rancisco Pride Band\nJoin the San Francisco Pride Band’s marching band a
 t the 2026 SF Veterans Day Parade as we honor those who have served. The p
 arade starts at 11:00 AM on Sunday\, November 8\, 2026\, at the Embarcader
 o and North Point Street\, then heads west along Jefferson Street to Aquat
 ic Park.\nFor the best view\, stand on Jefferson Street at Leavenworth Str
 eet\, where the reviewing stand is. You’ll hear the announcer introduce 
 each group\, including us. For a more relaxed spot\, watch from Jefferson 
 Street between Taylor and Jones Streets\, close to the Wharf’s food stan
 ds and shops. The parade\, officially called the San Francisco Mayor’s S
 alute to Veterans\, is free and open to everyone.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: http
 s://www.sfmta.com/travel-updates/veterans-day-parade-sunday-november-8-202
 6\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/veterans-day-parade-sf/\nSource: Funch
