BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CULTURE & DIVERSITY FILM FESTIVAL: Short Films on "Love\, Food & F
 reedom" and "Sports\, Dreams & Sailing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T180000
DTSTAMP:20261110T072652Z
UID:dothebay-17997410@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Culture & Diversity Film Festival presents:\n\nSHORT FILMS on 
 “LOVE\, FOOD & FREEDOM”\n\nKosherSoul\n\nCulinary historian and author
  Michael Twitty brings together a diverse team of chefs of color to presen
 t a historic communal meal rooted in African American\, Jewish\, and diasp
 oric culinary traditions in this Silver Telly Award-winning documentary fi
 lm.\n\nMise en Place\n\nVeteran dramatic filmmaker Andrew Kadikian present
 s the story of a chef who has lost his passion but finds new inspiration i
 n an unexpected place.\n\nVariety Club\n\nDesperate to grow up and leave a
  camp for kids with disabilities\, a young woman with Down syndrome plots 
 her escape with a potential suitor.\n\nDeepa\n\nA woman nearing 60 with de
 ep ties to her community in a thriving and active South Asian neighborhood
  comes to terms with emotions of love and loss.\n\nLove Will Set You Free\
 n\nA group of actors workshop and then present a musical stage play explor
 ing the meaning of the “Antebellum\, Interracial\, Intergenerational\, I
 ntersectional\, Fully Sexual\, Unbelievably True Tale of How the Power of 
 Love Will You Free.”\n\nalso\n\nSHORT DOCUMENTARIES on “SPORTS\, DREAM
 S & SAILING”\n\nShuttle\n\nA Thai badminton player takes on the challeng
 es of a sports scholarship in Beijing along with academic and family strug
 gles in passionate pursuit of a dream.\n\nGrassroots Drifter\n\nA teenage 
 driver is born to drift. This sport of drifting is gaining traction in Chi
 na\, with drivers of all ages pursuing the exhilarating compe00on of two c
 ars dramaticall...\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/9/cultu
 re-diversity-film-festival-short-films-on-love-food-freedom-and-sports-dre
 ams-sailing-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.782364;-122.482951
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35142047/f0db2d00-3ede-42e8-9968-a74bb0c584ff.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261110T072652Z
LOCATION:4 Star Theater\, 2200 Clement St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/9/culture-diversity-film-festival-
 short-films-on-love-food-freedom-and-sports-dreams-sailing-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:French Café Music dinner concert with Bistro Moustache
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T190000
DTSTAMP:20261110T072652Z
UID:dothebay-18029748@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Bistro Moustache plays French Café music\, a style that mixes
  Manouche\, Gypsy Jazz\, Musette\, Swing\, and that was popular in France 
 before and after the Second World War\, and that is still very much alive 
 today.\n\nWe go from the popular timeless classics (Les Feuilles Mortes\, 
 C’est Si Bon\, Ménilmontant\, J’Attendrai\, La Foule\, Sous Le Ciel D
 e Paris\, La Vie En Rose) to more modern (Il Est Cinq Heures Paris S’Év
 eille\, Le Poinçonneur Des Lilas\, Le Déserteur\, Vesoul)\, and even son
 gs that you may hear on the French radio today. We also feature dance tune
 s\, Waltzes\, Polkas\, Tangos\, Auvergne Bourrées and Celtic folk\, or Fr
 ench children comptines\, like Frère Jacques\, or Sur Le Pont D’Avignon
 . All the songs are sung in French by Olivier\, a native Parisian.\n\nJust
  as if Charles Trenet\, Jacques Brel\, Yves Montand\, Georges Brassens\, S
 erge Gainsbourg\, Tino Rossi\, Edith Piaf\, Boris Vian\, Django Reinhardt\
 , Gus Viseur and Jo Privat were all on the same stage together for one eve
 ning.\n\nPrepare to be musically transported to the terrace of a Paris Bis
 tro\, a Guinguette on the Marne river or a Bal Musette on the banks of the
  Seine.\n\nMore info at: http://www.bistromoustache.com/calendar\n\nFree\n
 \nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/9/french-cafe-music-dinner-
 with-bistro-moustache-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.788182;-122.440667
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35276283/ccd5e460-0b08-48f1-b0a0-166b12b09caf.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261110T072652Z
LOCATION:Scopo Divino\, 2800 California Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 9411
 5
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/9/french-cafe-music-dinner-with-bi
 stro-moustache-tickets
END:VEVENT
