BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Naza
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T200000
DTSTAMP:20261110T072652Z
UID:dothebay-18016705@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:NAZA is also playing at NEW PEOPLE\n\nIn secret conversations 
 on the rooftops of Tel Aviv at night\, the systems behind Israel’s calcu
 lated mass killing of Palestinian civilians in Gaza are revealed by the pe
 ople who designed and operated them.\n\nDirectors Note:\n\nWe made this fi
 lm out of a sense of obligation to use our position as Israeli filmmakers 
 and journalists to examine the systems behind the mass killing of Palestin
 ian civilians for which our country is responsible. While filming members 
 of Israel’s military on rooftops at night in Tel Aviv over the past thre
 e years\, we found ourselves asking the very questions that were asked by 
 our grandparents’ generation and throughout the 20th century: how does o
 ne group of people allow the total dehumanisation of another?\n\nWhat do t
 he inner workings of such a system look like? Many of the revelations in t
 he film were published almost immediately as we learned of them\, in the m
 onths following the October 7th attacks\, by The Guardian (one of NAZA’s
  producers)\, in collaboration with reporting partners +972 Magazine and L
 ocal Call. The film lets us explore something deeper than we could in our 
 investigative journalism alone: not only the words being said but also tho
 se that are not said\, the silence. It is up to all of us to break that si
 lence.\n\n– Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor\n\n“An essential\, devastati
 ng documentary…there’s no turning away from what’s said\, you simply
  can’t unknow what you have heard” – Nicolas Rapold\, Sight and Soun
 d...\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/9/naza-tickets\nSourc
 e: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35226199/eff8c639-81e1-47b7-bb24-542c49ae5546.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261110T072652Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/9/naza-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fatherland
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T200000
DTSTAMP:20261110T072652Z
UID:dothebay-18016726@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:FATHERLAND centres on the relationship between the Nobel Prize
 -winning writer Thomas Mann (Hanns Zischler) and his daughter Erika (Sandr
 a Hüller) – actress\, writer and rally driver. In the summer of 1949\, 
 at the height of the Cold War\, father and daughter embark on a challengin
 g and emotional road trip in a black Buick taking them across a Germany in
  ruins – from US dominated Frankfurt to Soviet controlled Weimar. Return
 ing home after sixteen years of exile in the US\, Thomas Mann has to face 
 not only a divided fatherland\, but also a deep fracture within his own fa
 mily.\n\nWith FATHERLAND\, director Paweł Pawlikowski picks up where he l
 eft off with his award-winning IDA and COLD WAR\, exploring – in his ell
 iptic\, distilled style – the themes of identity\, family\, love and gui
 lt amid the turmoil and confusion of post-war Europe.\n\n“Another expans
 ive\, enriching work from a modern master” – Time Out\n\n“A rich and
  moving journey through post-World War II Germany” – TheWrap\n\nMore s
 howtimes will be added soon.\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 22m\n\nYear\n\n2026\n\nDirec
 tor\n\nPaweł Pawlikowski\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nCountry\n\nPoland\, Germany\
 , Italy & France\n\nLanguage\n\nGerman\, French\, Russian & English\n\nFir
 st Showing\n\nNovember 6\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nOpen Caption Screenings\n
 \n\,\n\nFeatured\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/9/fatherl
 and-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35226312/c93649ad-e2bd-4bdd-b708-99bc61de7997.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261110T072652Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/9/fatherland-tickets
END:VEVENT
