SUMMARY:Japanese Tea Garden’s Free Admission Hour (Golden Gate Park)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T100000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1638818@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Outdoors
DESCRIPTION:Japanese Tea Garden’s Free Admission Hour (Golden Gate Park)
 \nJapanese Tea Garden\nThe Japanese Tea Garden provides visitors from arou
 nd the world with an opportunity to experience the natural beauty\, tranqu
 ility\, and harmony of a Japanese-style garden in the heart of San Francis
 co’s Golden Gate Park.\nOriginally created as a “Japanese Village” e
 xhibit for the 1894 California Midwinter International Exposition\, the Ja
 panese Tea Garden endures as one of the most popular attractions in San Fr
 ancisco\, featuring classic elements such as an arched drum bridge\, pagod
 as\, stone lanterns\, stepping stone paths\, native Japanese plants\, sere
 ne koi ponds\, and a zen garden. Cherry blossom trees bloom throughout the
  garden in March and April.\nAdmission to the Japanese Tea Garden is free 
 for San Francisco residents with valid ID. Free hours for everyone (even n
 on-residents) are 9-10 am every Monday\, Wednesday and Friday.\n\nPlease n
 ote that hours and costs change frequently.\nJapanese Tea Garden\n75 Hagiw
 ara Tea Garden\, Golden Gate Park\, SF\nFREE for San Francisco Residents w
 / ID\nFREE for Everyone from 9-10 am on Mondays\, Wednesdays and Fridays\n
 Non Resident Fees\nAdults: Tickets start at $16 (depends on season)\nSenio
 rs (ages 65+ w/ID) $7\nYouth (ages 12-17) $7\nChildren (ages 5-11) $3\nChi
 ldren (under 5) FREE\nOpen Daily at 9am-Last Entry\nLast entry is 30 minut
 es before closing. Last entry changes seasonally.\nSpring – Summer Last 
 Entry\nMarch – October: 5:30pm\nFall – Winter Last Entry\nNovember –
  February:...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.japaneseteagardensf.com/vist
 \nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/japanese-tea-gardens-free-admission-hou
 r-golden-gate-park-453/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/japane
 seteagarden-scaled-e1595352236641.jpeg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Japanese Tea Garden\, 75 Hagiwara Tea Garden Dr\, San Francisco\,
  CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/japanese-tea-gardens-free-admission-hour-golde
 n-gate-park-453/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beaver Bauer’s 50-Year Show of Art + Theater Costumes (SF Main L
 ibary)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T200000
DTSTAMP:20261111T063824Z
UID:funcheap-1640467@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lgbtq
DESCRIPTION:Danile Nicoletta PhotographyBeaver Bauer: From Street to Stage
 \, a Fifty-Year Retrospective by iconic artist and theatrical costume desi
 gner Beaver Bauer opens on Thurs. Nov. 5\, 2026 at 5:00 pm (Light snacks a
 nd beverages will be served)\nand runs thru Sun. April 11\, 2027 at the Sa
 n Francisco Public Library Main Branch – 100 Larkin St.\, San Francisco\
 , CA 94102. The show will be installed in the Jewett Gallery and Koret Lob
 by (Lower Level) and is FREE and open to the public during regular library
  hours.\nSFPL MAIN Hours: Tues. – Thurs.: 9:00 am – 8:00 pm\; Fri. –
  Sun.: Noon – 6:00 pm\nTRANSIT: Near Civic Center BART/Muni station. Bus
  Lines 5\, 6\, 7\, 9\, 21\, 47\, 49 stop within 4 blocks of the library.\n
 Beaver Bauer: From Street to Stage opens on Thurs.\, Nov. 5\, 2026 at 5:00
  pmat the San Francisco Public Library – Jewett Gallery on\, and runs th
 rough Sun. April 11\, 2027. This retrospective exhibition surveys the care
 er of Debra “Beaver” Bauer – the beloved and irreverent artist and c
 ostume designer that spans more than fifty years of creative work. the exh
 ibition includes original renderings\, performance photography\, video cli
 ps and elements from costumes drawn from her expansive work. Bauer develop
 ed her reputation first as a member of the experimental Angels of Light Fr
 ee Theater [working alongside celebrated performers such as: Hibiscus\, Ro
 dney Price and Martin Wong]\,which flourished for ten years before its cas
 t was impacted by AIDS. Their visual extravagance became her signature sty
 ...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://beaverbauer.com\nDetails: https://sf.funch
 eap.com/beaver-bauers-50year-show-art-theater-costumes-sf-main-libary/\nSo
 urce: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Front-
 of-post-card-BB-final-copy.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111T063824Z
LOCATION:San Francisco Public Library (SFPL) Main Library\, 100 Larkn St\,
  San Francisco CA 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/beaver-bauers-50year-show-art-theater-costumes
 -sf-main-libary/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:USS Hornet Veterans Day 2026 (Alameda)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T170000
DTSTAMP:20261111T063824Z
UID:funcheap-1645237@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art Museums
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerUSS HornetPlease join us at th
 e USS Hornet as we commemorate Veterans Day.\nOur main program will start 
 at 11 AM:\n\nColor Guard provided by: Civil Air Patrol\, US Air Force Auxi
 liary\nMC Robert Butchart (USAF Ret.)\nBio: Robert entered the United Stat
 es Air Force in 1982. He served in Air Force Special Operations and in the
  United States Joint Service Special Operations Command\; his last militar
 y assignment was in Central America with Navy Special Warfare\, 2002. Robe
 rt’s secondary specialty code in the military was a Chaplain’s Assista
 nt. Currently\, Robert is assigned to the California Governor’s Office o
 f Emergency Services (Cal OES)\; Robert is responsible for starting the Ma
 ritime Program for Cal OES.\nKeynote Speaker Michael Baker (USN Ret.)\nBio
 : Michael Baker is a retired general\, vascular\, trauma surgeon and retir
 ed US Navy Rear Admiral. He is a widely known as a speaker in the Bay Area
  for Commonwealth Club/World Affairs\, as a teacher for Osher LifeLong Lea
 rning on history\, political science\, and military affairs at Cal State E
 ast Bay and UC Berkeley\, and still teaches combat casualty care at US Mil
 itary bases and has completed 5 tours in Ukraine teaching Advanced Trauma 
 Life Support (ATLS).\nWe will finish with a wreath laying at the fantail.\
 n—————————————————-\nIn the afternoon we
  will have a presentation at 1 PM:\nJeremy Holm (US Army Ret.) will presen
 t “Rescue at Los Baños: One of World War II’s Greatest Rescue Mission
 s.”\nOn February 23\, 1945\,...\n\n$25.00\n\nTickets: https://uss-hornet
 .org/event/veterans-day-2026/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/uss-hornet
 -veterans-day-2026-alameda/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/the-us
 s-hornet-sea-air-2.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111T063824Z
LOCATION:USS Hornet Sea\, Air & Space Museum\, 707 W. Hornet Avenue\, Alam
 eda\, Ca
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/uss-hornet-veterans-day-2026-alameda/
END:VEVENT
