DESCRIPTION:DarkParlourSocietyEvery Wednesday\, Dark Parlour Society turns
  Spire\, a century-old church in West Oakland\, into a candlelit parlour f
 or junk journaling. Cut\, collage\, glue and make something strange while 
 a vintage picture show plays on the big screen. The film is atmosphere\, n
 ot homework: talk\, wander and work at your own pace.\nPapers\, scraps\, s
 cissors and glue are on the tables. Bring your own journal\, scraps or yar
 n to share\, or bring nothing at all.\nThis season’s pictures:\nWed\, No
 v 11: Nosferatu (1922)\, with Hugh Doolan’s orchestral score\nWed\, Nov 
 18: House on Haunted Hill (1959)\, with Vincent Price\nWed\, Nov 25: Chara
 de (1963)\, with Audrey Hepburn and Cary Grant\nWed\, Dec 9: Santa Claus C
 onquers the Martians (1964)\n6 to 8 PM. Spire\, 825 Athens Ave\, Oakland.\
 nFree. 18+. Supplies provided. Donations go to Spire.\nRSVP at darkparlour
 society.com/rsvp\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.darkparloursociety.com\nD
 etails: https://sf.funcheap.com/glue-stick-social-junk-journaling-glow-cre
 epy-picture-show-oakland-2/\nSource: Funcheap SF
