BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ólafur Arnalds
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T210000
DTSTAMP:20261104T012711Z
UID:dothebay-16881125@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:2nd Show Added by Popular Demand!\n\nAnother Planet Entertainm
 ent Presents\nÓlafur Arnalds\nWednesday\, November 11 | The Castro\n\nAwa
 rd-winning artist\, composer and producer Ólafur Arnalds returns with his
  most daring and adventurous project to date.\n\nFalling Apart Together is
  an attempt at dismantling the distance between us. A concert hybrid that 
 reveals the layers we construct in order to feel safe\, the moments in whi
 ch those layers tremble and the sense of intimacy and shared humanity that
  emerges when we allow ourselves to be exposed.\n\nTogether with his team 
 of devoted craftsmen and musicians\, Ólafur presents a spellbinding blend
  of past and new material in a show that challenges the boundaries of what
  a concert can be.\n\nAfter his globally acclaimed tours following re:memb
 er and some kind of peace — which sold out such iconic halls as Royal Al
 bert Hall\, Elbphilharmonie\, Sydney Opera House\, and Walt Disney Concert
  Hall – performing to hundreds of thousands of fans worldwide — Ólafu
 r returns with his most intimate and boundary-pushing work to date.\n\nFal
 ling Apart Together explores what becomes possible when we let ourselves u
 nravel just enough to collectively open up.\n\nAll ages\nSold out\nAnother
  Planet Entertainment Presents - 2nd Show Added by Popular Demand!\nListed
  time is doors\n\nTickets: https://ticketmaster.evyy.net/c/253185/264167/4
 272?SharedId=DoStuff&u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ticketmaster.com%2Folafur-arnalds
 -san-francisco-california-11-11-2026%2Fevent%2F1C006425D688A714%3Fcamefrom
 %3DCFC_ANOTHERPLANET_web%26brand%3Danotherplanet\nDetails: https://dotheba
 y.com/events/2026/11/11/olafur-arnalds-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7619917;-122.4347365
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/29848825/5a127cd8-5644-4f90-99df-3f6dc4620dfc.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T012711Z
LOCATION:The Castro\, 429 Castro St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94114
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/11/olafur-arnalds-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Holy Wave
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T210000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17409510@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:In Ensenada\, Mexico\, where the Pacific horizon cuts a clean\
 , unwavering line\, Holy Wave recorded their latest full length\, i’m DA
 DA\, a record that feels both expansive and newly concentrated for the sub
 terranean pop four-piece. Stepping outside the United States was less a re
 treat than a shift in perspective\, creating distance to recognize a new s
 ound that had been slowly taking shape among them. i’m DADA quickly reve
 aled its character: more propulsive\, more candid\, and their most structu
 rally deliberate work to date.\n\nWorking alongside experimental duo Lorel
 le Meets the Obsolete at their studio El Derrumbe the sessions folded comm
 unity into the album\, though its emotional core had already formed over m
 onths of pre-production. Half of Holy Wave is Mexican\, with roots in the 
 El Paso border region\, so recording in Ensenada felt intuitive and relaxe
 d. Joo Joo Ashworth\, mixing engineer and longtime friend\, also provided 
 a pivotal presence helping crystallize the album’s rhythmic language and
  subtly expanding the band’s sound. The songs began reflecting conversat
 ions about fatherhood and partnership\, breakups and estrangement\, the qu
 easy acceleration of AI\, and what it means to remain present and principl
 ed while the world lurches unpredictably forward.\n\nPresented by Kilowatt
 .\n\nThis is a 21+ event\n\n$24.72\, 21+\nPresented by Kilowatt.\n\nTicket
 s: https://link.dice.fm/Y5fe9e3cffee?pid=717f1d8a\nDetails: https://dotheb
 ay.com/events/2026/11/11/holy-wave-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7650767;-122.423278
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/32366787/589bad12-3d2a-444e-bcad-a07f59e8945a.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Kilowatt\, 3160 16th St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/11/holy-wave-tickets
END:VEVENT
