DESCRIPTION:As workers and as parents\, we all care deeply about how we mu
 st prepare ourselves and our children for fulfilling careers at a time whe
 n the changing nature of labor is opaque.\nIn this interactive book talk\,
  co-author Illah Nourbakhsh will share brief remarks regarding our voyage 
 in researching and writing a book about careers\, AI and the future of edu
 cation. We will be joined by two special pioneers who will make brief rema
 rks from the audience: Alan Eustace and Professor Michael Genesereth.\nAla
 n Eustace served as senior vice president at Google and has witnessed the 
 digital and AI technology revolutions firsthand. Michael Genesereth is fac
 ulty at Stanford University and charted the course of artificial intellige
 nce research as one of its founding scholars.\nBoth Alan and Michael care 
 deeply about the next generation\, and the ways in which careers will evol
 ve as AI changes the shape of work.\n\nWe look forward to a dynamic conver
 sation with the audience.\n\nFree\nBook Passage Presents:\n\nTickets: http
 s://bookpassage.com/event/illah-nourbakhsh-crunch-time\nDetails: https://d
 othebay.com/events/2026/11/12/illah-nourbakhsh-crunch-time-tickets\nSource
 : DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/illah-nourbakhsh-
 crunch-time/
