BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chronotope Opening Reception
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T200000
DTSTAMP:20261111T063824Z
UID:funcheap-1646344@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art Museums
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerJacques VILLEGLÉ [1926-2022]\
 , "Rue Pastourelle\," 23 avril 1972\, décollage mounted on canvasGROUP EX
 HIBITION INCLUDING: PETER ALEXANDER | MARKUS BAENZIGER | PIERRE BURAGLIO |
  LAUREN DICIOCCIO | MICHAEL EASTMAN | JONATHON KEATS | FRANÇOIS KOLLAR | 
 TANJA RECTOR | JOHN REGISTER | WARD SCHUMAKER | LOUIS STETTNER | HIROSHI S
 UGIMOTO | ILOND TANSOVSKAYA | JACQUES VILLEGLÉ | MAX YAVNO\nTHE PUBLIC IS
  INVITED TO AN OPENING RECEPTION THURSDAY\, NOVEMBER 12\, FROM 6:00-8:00PM
 \n\nModernism is pleased to present Chronotope\, a group exhibition featur
 ing works by 15 artists across painting\, photography\, sculpture\, printm
 aking and décollage.\nMeaning literally “time-space\,” chronotope is 
 a term introduced by Russian literary theorist Mikhail Bakhtin [1895–197
 5] to describe the intrinsic connection between temporal and spatial relat
 ionships. Developed in the intellectual aftermath of Russian Modernism and
  the avant-garde\, the concept was influenced by Einstein’s theory of re
 lativity and its understanding of time and space as inseparable dimensions
 . Bakhtin adapted this idea to literature\, proposing that time becomes pe
 rceptible through space and that space\, in turn\, bears the evidence of t
 ime.\nChronotope extends this relationship to visual art\, examining how a
 rtists capture time through images of places\, objects and environments. C
 locks\, theaters\, storefronts\, streets and landscapes become symbols of 
 both physical location and temporal experience.\nCentral to the exhibi...\
 n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://modernisminc.com/exhibitions/CHRONOTOPE--GROUP
 _EXHIBITION/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/chronotope-opening-receptio
 n/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Villeg
 le.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111T063824Z
LOCATION:Modernism\, 724 Ellis Street\, San Francisco. CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/chronotope-opening-reception/
END:VEVENT
