SUMMARY:Panel: Mother Jones-50 Years of Fearless Journalism
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T203000
DTSTAMP:20261111T063824Z
UID:dothebay-17999229@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Activism
DESCRIPTION:Learn more about San Francisco's rich journalism history with 
 an engaging discussion about the nation's first investigative news organiz
 ation\, Mother Jones\, which started in 1976 in an office above a McDonald
 's restaurant in San Francisco. As a special bonus\, the panelists analyze
  the November 3 election results and the news media's coverage of the big 
 races and issues\, particularly in California.\n\nSitting on the panel are
  Mother Jones' editor-in-chief Clara Jeffery and Mother Jones' co-founder 
 and historian Adam Hochschild. Journalist Jamil Smith moderates.\n\nA cate
 red reception precedes the panel discussion from 5-6:30 in the Koret Lobby
 . While you're here\, you can also visit the 50 Years of Mother Jones exhi
 bit on the 5th floor in the Magazines and Newspapers Center!\n\nFree\n\nPr
 esented by San Francisco Public Library\n\nFree\nSan Francisco Public Libr
 ary\n\nTickets: https://on.sfpl.org/MotherJones\nDetails: https://dothebay
 .com/events/2026/11/12/panel-mother-jones-50-years-of-fearless-journalism-
 tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/fr
 ee-mother-jones-50th-anniversary-journalism-panel-sf-main-library/
