DESCRIPTION:HACDrinks\, bites\, and a post-election debrief hosted by the 
 Housing Action Coalition\, SF YIMBY\, and Alex Clemens of Progress Public 
 Affairs\nElection day will have passed\, the ballots counted (we hope\, it
 ’s ranked-choice)\, and we’re ready to break it all down. Join us at H
 arrington’s\, a downtown watering hole since 1935\, to talk through what
  happened on November 3rd and what it means for housing in San Francisco a
 nd across California.\nWe’ll cover:\n\nThe supervisor races and ballot m
 easures in San Francisco\nThe statewide results and the new faces heading 
 to City Hall and Sacramento\nWhat it all means for getting more homes buil
 t\, and the fights coming in 2027\n\nExpect quick takes\, honest predictio
 ns\, and at least one person still explaining their ranked-choice ballot. 
 Grab a drink and some food\, and come talk shop with fellow housing advoca
 tes\, builders\, and neighbors.\nOpen to all. Bring a friend. See you Thur
 sday November 12th at 6:30pm\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://actionnetwork.org
 /events/hac-sf-yimby-progress-pa-election-recap-at-harringtons?source=soci
 al\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/free-sf-postelection-debrief-housing-
 ballot-results-sf/\nSource: Funcheap SF
