BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What is a Public Intellectual Today: Alexis Madrigal
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T200000
DTSTAMP:20261111T063824Z
UID:funcheap-1645518@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lectures Workshops
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerMiya HirabayashiStanford Publi
 c Humanities invites Bay Area community members to the autumn event of the
 ir flagship series\, “What is a Public Intellectual Today\,” which wil
 l feature journalist Alexis Madrigal in conversation with professor Adrian
  Daub on craft\, career\, and culture in the Bay Area and beyond. The even
 t will include audience Q&A and book selling/signing to follow!\nAlexis Ma
 drigal is an acclaimed multimedia journalist in Oakland\, CA. He is the co
 -host of KQED’s current affairs show Forum\, creator of the 8-part podca
 st Containers\, author of the newsletter The Oakland Garden Club\, and a c
 ontributing writer at The Atlantic. His book The Pacific Circuit explores 
 how a logistical revolution that began in Oakland has reshaped American ci
 ties. He is the proprietor of Local Economy\, a community space in Oakland
 \, and has been a visiting scholar at UC Berkeley’s School of Informatio
 n and the Center for Science\, Technology\, Medicine & Society.\n\nAdrian 
 Daub is the J.E. Wallace Sterling Professor in the Humanities at Stanford 
 University\, where he serves as the Faculty Director of the Clayman Instit
 ute for Gender Research. He is the author of What Tech Calls Thinking (202
 0) and The Cancel Culture Panic (2024)\, and writes for numerous US and Eu
 ropean newspapers and magazines.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://events.stanfo
 rd.edu/event/what-is-a-public-intellectual-today-alexis-madrigal\nDetails:
  https://sf.funcheap.com/public-intellectual-today-alexis-madrigal/\nSourc
 e: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/@hey_m
 iya-a-madrigal-proofs-062624-11.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111T063824Z
LOCATION:Tresidder Oak Lounge / Stanford University\, 498 Santa Teresa Str
 eet\, Stanford
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/public-intellectual-today-alexis-madrigal/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ólafur Arnalds
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T210000
DTSTAMP:20261104T012711Z
UID:dothebay-16822925@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Another Planet Entertainment Presents\nÓlafur Arnalds\nThursd
 ay\, November 12 | The Castro\n\nAward-winning artist\, composer and produ
 cer Ólafur Arnalds returns with his most daring and adventurous project t
 o date.\n\nFalling Apart Together is an attempt at dismantling the distanc
 e between us. A concert hybrid that reveals the layers we construct in ord
 er to feel safe\, the moments in which those layers tremble and the sense 
 of intimacy and shared humanity that emerges when we allow ourselves to be
  exposed.\n\nTogether with his team of devoted craftsmen and musicians\, 
 Ólafur presents a spellbinding blend of past and new material in a show t
 hat challenges the boundaries of what a concert can be.\n\nAfter his globa
 lly acclaimed tours following re:member and some kind of peace — which s
 old out such iconic halls as Royal Albert Hall\, Elbphilharmonie\, Sydney 
 Opera House\, and Walt Disney Concert Hall – performing to hundreds of t
 housands of fans worldwide — Ólafur returns with his most intimate and 
 boundary-pushing work to date.\n\nFalling Apart Together explores what bec
 omes possible when we let ourselves unravel just enough to collectively op
 en up.\n\nAll ages\nSold out\nAnother Planet Entertainment Presents\nListe
 d time is doors\n\nTickets: https://ticketmaster.evyy.net/c/253185/264167/
 4272?SharedId=DoStuff&u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ticketmaster.com%2Folafur-arnald
 s-san-francisco-california-11-12-2026%2Fevent%2F1C006425D68AA716%3Fcamefro
 m%3DCFC_ANOTHERPLANET_web%26brand%3Danotherplanet\nDetails: https://dotheb
 ay.com/events/2026/11/12/olafur-arnalds-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7619917;-122.4347365
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/29566459/1f8d5af4-4430-4bb5-9ad8-e366938ed3ec.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T012711Z
LOCATION:The Castro\, 429 Castro St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94114
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/12/olafur-arnalds-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening With Band of Horses
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T190000
