BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Max Jaffe: You Want That Too! + Burden of Dreams
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T103000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17845411@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Variety
DESCRIPTION:Buy Tickets\n\nDoors 8pm / Show 8:30pm\n\n$23 / free or discou
 nted for members\n\nIn a trio formation with some of the core rhythm secti
 on players from the record\, Max Jaffe\, Gavin Gamboa\, and Logan Kane rei
 magine the music from Jaffe's 2025 release You Want That Too!\n\nMax Jaffe
  is a drummer\, producer\, composer\, and technologist based in Los Angele
 s\, CA. His work expands the possibilities of composition and collaboratio
 n through the drum set.\n\nIn 2025\, Jaffe released "You Want That Too!" o
 n Colorfield Records. Eclectic and tuneful\, the album received praise fro
 m Pitchfork and is being followed with a series of special live performanc
 es in varying formations.\n\nMax is a founding member of experimental rock
  collective JOBS\, Amirtha Kidambi's Elder Ones\, and several others. He h
 as toured\, performed\, and recorded with many diverse artists including W
 ild Up\, Steph Richards\, Nels Cline\, Ava Mendoza\, Cass McCombs\, DARKSI
 DE\, Normal Love\, Jeff Parker\, Vinny Golia\, Peter Evans\, and many othe
 rs.\n\nBurden of Dreams is the latest band from Oakland composer and multi
 -instrumentalist\, Nathan Clevenger. Along with Clevenger on electric bass
 \, the ensemble features Brett Carson (Hammond organ)\, Mark Pascucci-Clif
 ford (vibraphone)\, and Jason Levis (drums). The band's music is dark and 
 dense\, drawing from 20th Century classical\, doom rock\, and jazz.\n\nPho
 to by Alex De La Hidalga.\n\n$23\n\nTickets: https://link.dice.fm/a5174866
 35f7\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/14/max-jaffe-you-want-t
 hat-too-burden-of-dreams-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.765289;-122.418493
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34433863/23afda00-c1b2-41a7-ac67-58af1198537f.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:The Lab\, 2948 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/14/max-jaffe-you-want-that-too-bur
 den-of-dreams-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trail & Habitat Volunteer Work: Restoring Laguna Honda’s Lost Tr
 ails | SF
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T120000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1637021@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Outdoors
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerTrail & Habitat Volunteer Work
 : Restoring Laguna Honda’s Lost Trails | SF\nSF Urban Riders\nDid you kn
 ow that there’s another trail system in San Francisco? The trails have b
 een off the radar for some time. SF Urban Riders is proud to announce that
  they’re working with the Laguna Honda Hospital and Rehabilitation Cente
 r in improving the historic multi­ use trails.\nThis effort engages the c
 ommunity and new volunteers to build the trail\, it also creates a new des
 tination for visitors\, is an asset to the Hospital community\, and will b
 ecome part of the larger San Francisco trail system that connects people i
 n the City to a wild\, inviting and educational open space.\n\nTrail & Hab
 itat Volunteer Work: Restoring Laguna Honda’s Lost Trails\nEvery 2nd Sat
 urday | 9 am to 12 nn\nLaguna Honda Hospital\, 375 Laguna Honda Blvd.\, SF
 \, CA\nFREE\n– Updated 6/4/19 – Event info last checked via website\n\
 nUpcoming Trail & Habitat Volunteer Work: Restoring Laguna Honda’s Lost 
 Trails | SF Events\nSat 10/10 Trail & Habitat Volunteer Work: Restoring La
 guna Honda’s Lost Trails | SFSat 11/14 Trail & Habitat Volunteer Work: R
 estoring Laguna Honda’s Lost Trails | SFSat 12/12 Trail & Habitat Volunt
 eer Work: Restoring Laguna Honda’s Lost Trails | SFDisclaimer: Please do
 uble check event information with the event organizer as events can be can
 celed\, details can change after they are added to our calendar\, and erro
 rs do occur.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: http://sfurbanriders.org/laguna-honda-hos
 pital-project/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/trail-habitat-volunteer-w
 ork-restoring-laguna-hondas-lost-trails-sf-108/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/Screen
 -Shot-2018-09-07-at-11.33.36-PM.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Laguna Honda Hospital\, 375 Laguna Honda Blvd\, San Francisco\, C
