BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Indigenous Voices: Sara Calvosa Olson and Crystal Wahpepah in Conv
 ersation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T203000
DTSTAMP:20261111T063824Z
UID:dothebay-18029372@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Literature
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we continue our Native American Heritage Month seri
 es\, welcoming Sara Calvosa Olson and Crystal Wahpepah to share their late
 st works — Chími Nu'am and A Feather and a Fork.\n\nFree to attend — 
 RSVP required to reserve your seat.\n\nSpeakers\nSara Calvosa Olson (Karuk
 ) is a food writer and editor living in the Bay Area with her husband and 
 two teenage sons. Her work dwells at the intersection of storytelling\, In
 digenous food systems\, security\, sovereignty\, reconnection\, and recipe
  development. Her writing has appeared in News from Native California and 
 Edible Shasta-Butte. Visit her website at akihsara.com\, and follow her on
  Instagram at @thefrybreadriot.\n\nChef Crystal Wahpepah\, a registered me
 mber of the Kickapoo Tribe of Oklahoma\, has long been a warrior for Indig
 enous food sovereignty. She is the creative tour de force behind the inven
 tive\, healthy\, and delicious dishes served at her restaurant\, Wahpepah
 ’s Kitchen\, in Oakland\, California—the first Native woman-owned rest
 aurant in Northern California.\nIf Crystal is not at her Oakland\, Califor
 nia restaurant\, Wahpepah’s Kitchen\, she is on the road\, talking about
  Native American foodways\, advocating for Indigenous food sovereignty\, a
 nd celebrating the launch of her debut cookbook\, “A Feather and a Fork.
 ”\n\nFree\nTelegraph Hill Arts and Literature Presents:\n\nTickets: http
 s://telhil.it/Sara-and-Crystal\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/
 11/14/indigenous-voices-sara-calvosa-olson-and-crystal-wahpepah-in-convers
 ation-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.
 com/native-american-heritage-month-free-author-talk-indigenous-foodways-sf
 /
GEO:37.800823;-122.407824
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35274564/680d3ba7-0b4c-4576-a9f0-99e0d74af903.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111T063824Z
LOCATION:Telegraph Hill Books\, 1501 Grant Avenue\, San Francisco\, CA\, 9
 4133
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/14/indigenous-voices-sara-calvosa-
 olson-and-crystal-wahpepah-in-conversation-tickets
END:VEVENT
