BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Philosophy Talk Live: Franz Kafka and the World Without a Path
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T210000
DTSTAMP:20261106T013613Z
UID:dothebay-18045400@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:Join KALW & Philosophy Talk with guest Karen Zumhagen-Yekplé\
 , for a deep dive into Kafka's world\, and what it has to say about ours.\
 n\nFranz Kafka is famous for his stunning\, unparalleled\, and often seari
 ng writings\, from novels like The Trial and The Castle to short stories l
 ike “The Metamorphosis” and “A Hunger Artist.” All of these fictio
 ns clearly engage with philosophy\, and they often seem to present a world
  without a clear path. Even as readers\, we often struggle to find a clear
  path\, something that would help us find our way in Kafka’s extraordina
 ry world. So what does Kafka actually believe? What can we learn by spendi
 ng time with his stories? And are they really trying to “teach” us som
 ething\, or is their philosophical gift to us something far more precious?
 \n\nJoin our live audience at KALW’s downtown event space as the Philoso
 phers record a brand-new episode with Karen Zumhagen-Yekplé\, Professor o
 f English and Comparative Literature at Tulane University and author of 
 “The Everyday’s Fabulous Beyond: Nonsense\, Parable\, and the Ethics o
 f the Literary in Kafka and Wittgenstein.”\n\nIn addition to thought-pro
 voking conversation and audience questions\, the show will feature multime
 dia reporting from our Roving Philosophical Reporter and satirical comment
 ary from Ian Shoales the Sixty-Second Philosopher.\n\nPart of the Jewish T
 hinkers series\, generously sponsored by Common Era.\n\nThis Episode's Gue
 st\nKaren Zumhagen-Yekplé is Associate Professor in the Department of Com
 parative L...\n\nFree\nKALW Public Media\n\nTickets: https://consumer.pxf.
 io/APvP5J?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.eventbrite.com%2Fe%2Fphilosophy-talk-live-fr
 anz-kafka-and-the-world-without-a-path-tickets-2002896450199%3Faff%3Doddtd
 tcreator\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/17/philosophy-talk-
 live-franz-kafka-and-the-world-without-a-path-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35343063/d133d7d5-4934-4d0a-9bdd-114f4676a30a.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261106T013613Z
LOCATION:KALW @ 220 Montgomery\, 220 Montgomery St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94104
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/17/philosophy-talk-live-franz-kafk
 a-and-the-world-without-a-path-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boynextdoor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T213000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17504898@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:If tickets in the accessible section are unavailable\, please 
 reach out to the venue for accommodations. Please note\, orders in violati
 on of the published ticket limit are subject to cancellation without notic
 e. Ticket prices may fluctuate\, at any time\, based on demand\n\nConsisti
 ng of members SUNGHO\, RIWOO\, JAEHYUN\, TAESAN\, LEEHAN and WOONHAK\, BOY
 NEXTDOOR are the first boy group to debut under KOZ ENTERTAINMENT\, founde
 d by artist-producer ZICO. Living up to their name as K-pop’s authentic 
 new wave\, the group turns everyday experiences into honest\, relatable so
 ngs that connect across generations. Their 1st EP WHY.. (September 2023) s
 aw the group make a strong entrance\, landing on the Billboard 200 and top
 ping the Billboard Emerging Artists Chart. Their 2nd EP HOW? (April 2024) 
 climbed to No. 93 on the Billboard 200 — a 69-step jump from their debut
 . Their 3rd EP 19.99 (September 2024) peaked at No. 40\, becoming their fi
 rst million-seller and topping the World Albums and Emerging Artists Chart
 s. Their digital single “IF I SAY\, I LOVE YOU” (January 2025) charted
  at No. 99 on the Billboard Global Excl. US and No. 188 on the Global 200\
