SUMMARY:LITQUAKE: Saira Mohamed - What a Country Owes Its Soldiers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T210000
DTSTAMP:20261106T013613Z
UID:dothebay-18045416@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Literature
DESCRIPTION:Join Mohamed as she discusses her new book\, arguing compassio
 nately for policies that convey genuine respect for soldiers’ humanity\n
 \nFREE\, $10–15 suggested donation\n\nCo-presented with KALW\n\nLegal sc
 holar Saira Mohamed has focused her career on the ethics of armed conflict
  and mass atrocity\, in particular on the legal obligations of governments
  around the world to protect and care for their military personnel. At a t
 ime when our own leaders publicly extol the contributions of soldiers and 
 veterans but strategically dismantle their support systems\, not to mentio
 n their sense of safety\, these questions—at the intersections of law an
 d ethics—are more essential than ever. Join Mohamed as she discusses her
  new book What a Country Owes Its Soldiers\, deeply informed by her resear
 ch and arguing compassionately for policies that convey genuine respect fo
 r soldiers’ humanity. In conversation with journalist and Pulitzer Prize
  finalist Aaron Glantz\, author of War Comes Home: Washington's Battle aga
 inst America's Veterans. Doors at 6:30pm.\n\nFree\nKALW Public Media\n\nTi
 ckets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.eventbrite.com%2
 Fe%2Fsaira-mohamed-what-a-country-owes-its-soldiers-tickets-1999212083158%
 3Faff%3Doddtdtcreator\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/18/lit
 quake-saira-mohamed-what-a-country-owes-its-soldiers-tickets\nSource: DoTh
 eBay
