BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Black Hammer’s Free “Hopped Up” Trivia Night (Every Wednesda
 y)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1638727@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Eating Drinking
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerBlack Hammer’s Free “Hoppe
 d Up” Trivia Night (Every Wednesday)\nBlack Hammer Brewing\nNo pens\, no
  paper.\nJoin us for three rounds of fast-paced gameshow-style pub trivia 
 in our taproom every Wednesday at 7PM. Free admission\, with bonus points 
 for fastest answer and a live scoreboard.\n\nHopped Up Trivia\nEvery Wedne
 sday at 7pm\nBlack Hammer Brewing\, 544 Bryant St\, SF\nFREE admission\nCh
 eck the website to make reservations and confirm the date.\nPrizes awarded
  for 1st\, 2nd and 3rd place finishers. Always cheer for fastest answer!\n
 Maximum team size is 8 people. Good natured trash-talking encouraged but n
 ot required.\nAbout Black Hammer Brewing\nBlack Hammer Brewing Company bre
 ws and serves award-winning gluten-removed beers that are indistinguishabl
 e from conventional gluten-containing brews. Our taproom\, which has been 
 described as “Cheers on LSD”\, features 16 fresh house-brewed beers on
  tap\, craft empanadas from El Sur\, frittatas (gluten free!) and quiches 
 from Nucha\, and warm soft pretzel sticks served with grain mustard from W
 illkommen\, as well many to-go options. We are dog friendly and offer indo
 or and heated outdoor seating with tons of street parking.\nGet to enjoy t
 heir award-winning beers while enjoying the night with friends!\n\nView th
 is post on Instagram\n\nA post shared by Black Hammer Brewing Company (@bl
 ackhammerbrewing)\n\nUpcoming Black Hammer’s Free “Hopped Up” Trivia
  Night (Every Wednesday) Events\nWed 10/7 Black Hammer’s Free “Hopped 
 Up” Trivia...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://bhb.beer/trivia\nDetails: http
 s://sf.funcheap.com/black-hammers-free-hopped-up-trivia-night-every-wednes
 day-146/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/Trivia
 _May23-23.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Black Hammer Brewing\, 544 Bryant St.\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/black-hammers-free-hopped-up-trivia-night-ever
 y-wednesday-146/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Astronomy Talk: Chile’s Giant Observatories (Randall Museum
 )
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T203000
DTSTAMP:20261105T110617Z
UID:funcheap-1645552@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lectures Workshops
DESCRIPTION:The San Francisco Amateur Astronomers invite you to this free 
 public event.\nChile is home to many of the largest and most advanced obse
 rvatories on Earth\, due to high altitudes\, dry deserts\, and low light p
 ollution. Chile has become a center of cutting edge astronomical research\
 , but this has been made possible by the collaborative efforts of multiple
  countries and the work of scientists and engineers from around the globe.
  This past summer I had the opportunity to participate in the Astronomy in
  Chile Educator Ambassadors Program (ACEAP). The program took me to the ma
 jor observatories (ALMA\, Vera Rubin\, Gemini South\, and more) and met ma
 ny of the people who keep the observatories running. I’ll be sharing my 
 insights into Chile\, international astronomical collaborations\, and the 
 southern skies.\nBrian “Astro” Castro is an amateur astronomer in San 
 Francisco known for his pop-up sidewalk astronomy events in The Mission\, 
 around SF\, and occasionally around the world. From 4” travel scopes tha
 t fit in a carry-on with room to spare\, to 16” Dobsonians\, he has show
 n the cosmos to over 15\,000 people. He has organized for the local chapte
 r of The Planetary Society\, solo traveled to Guatemala to personally dona
 te telescopes to schools and instruct in their use\, and even strapped a l
 arge telescope to a bicycle trailer and biked around showing Saturn to fes
 tival goers at Burning Man in the Black Rock Desert. He is a 2025 ACEAP Am
 bassador\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.sfaa-astronomy.org/public-events/
 lectures/lectures_2026/nov18_2026\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/free-a
 stronomy-talk-chiles-giant-observatories-randall-museum/\nSource: Funcheap
  SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ChileC
 astro.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261105T110617Z
LOCATION:Randall Museum\, 199 Museum Way\, San Francisco CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/free-astronomy-talk-chiles-giant-observatories
 -randall-museum/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Astronomy on Tap SF
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T210000
DTSTAMP:20261111T063824Z
UID:funcheap-1646687@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Eating Drinking
DESCRIPTION:AoT SF\n\nLocal astronomers talking about stars\, planets\, an
 d the universe at your neighborhood bar. No PhD required.\n\nAstronomy on 
 Tap is is a free public lecture series where astronomers give short\, laid
 -back talks over drinks at local bars. No background in science required 
 — our scientists share cool stuff about space while the audience sits ba
 ck and relaxes\, with plenty of time to indulge their curiosity and ask wh
 atever questions they want.\nThis month\, we’re hosting:\n\nLaura Schaef
 er (Stanford) – Exploring Lava Worlds with NASA’s James Webb Space Tel
 escope\nand\nCalvin Leung (UC Berkeley) – Finding the Missing Matter wit
 h Fast Radio Bursts\nSchaefer is an Associate Professor of Earth and Plane
 tary Sciences at Stanford\, and Leung is a Miller Fellow and former NASA E
 instein Fellow at UC Berkeley in the Department of Astronomy\, as well as 
 a member of the CHIME/FRB Collaboration.\nAstronomy on Tap takes place in 
 cities all over the world. This is a revival of the San Francisco chapter\
 , which regularly hosted events before the pandemic. We’re excited to be
  back on a monthly basis!\nNOTE: We are at Public Works this month\, with 
 more space for everyone! The event is still free\, but the venue will ask 
 you to fulfill the 1 drink minimum by buying a $13 drink ticket.\n\nFree\n
 \nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/astronomy-on-tap-sf-november-2026-
 tickets-2004626231020?\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/astronomy-tap-sf-
 2/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/aot-sf
 -nov-small.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111T063824Z
LOCATION:Public Works\, 161 Erie St.\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/astronomy-tap-sf-2/
END:VEVENT
