DESCRIPTION:What: The Story Exchange: An evening of sharing true stories &
  making connections\nWhen: Thursday\, November 19\, 6:00 PM - 7:30 PM\nWhe
 re: The Fold (map)\nTickets: Sliding scale tickets\, information below\n\n
 Description:\nForgot how to interact with people in the wild? Accidentally
  called your boss 'mom' in front of your coworkers and now you don’t kno
 w what to do with that? Considered making your dog your emergency contact?
  Deeply terrified that you’ll never experience true human connection bec
 ause your primary social outlet is arguing with strangers in subreddits? W
 ell then\, talking to actual humans at the Story Exchange may be right for
  you.\n\nMission StageWorks invites you to a guided storytelling experienc
 e where you can swap true stories and build actual\, real-time connections
 . We provide a supportive space and the story prompts\, so there's zero pr
 essure to perform (or be a stand-up comedian). Just an evening of meeting 
 people\, discovering you aren't the only one with deeply specific hang ups
 \, and finding community through meaningful conversations.\nMeet people 
 – tell stories – find your community – eat snacks\n\nFor more inform
 ation\, click here.\n\n$20-40 sliding scale\, 2-for-1 promo NOTAFLOF\nMiss
 ion StageWorks presents:\n\nTickets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=http
 s%3A%2F%2Fwww.eventbrite.com%2Fe%2Fthe-story-exchange-an-evening-of-sharin
 g-true-stories-making-connections-tickets-2003441352015\nDetails: https://
 dothebay.com/events/2026/11/19/the-story-exchange-an-evening-of-sharing-tr
 ue-stories-making-connections-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
