DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerSusan St. MartinFrom lament to
  light\, Tactus SF traces a journey of redemption in choral music spanning
  three centuries and two continents. From the waters of Babylon\, music of
  exile and grief\, the program turns slowly toward hope and ends in radian
 ce. Songs by Guillaume Dufay\, Tomás Luis de Victoria\, Juana de la Cruz\
 , Jean Mouton\, William Billings\, and others\, along with poetry readings
 \, describe a transformation from pain and darkness into light and love.\n
 A reception will follow each concert.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.even
 tbrite.com/e/t-r-a-n-s-c-e-n-d-e-n-c-e-san-francisco-tickets-2003269941321
 \nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/transcendence-free-choral-music-poetry-
