BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film: Defiant to the Last- Resistance at the Tule Lake Jail
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T210000
DTSTAMP:20261111T063824Z
UID:funcheap-1646534@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Movies
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerDefiant to the Last filmFilm S
 creening & Discussion of Defiant to the Last\, Resistance at the Tule Lake
  Jail\nwith Filmmaker Emiko Omori and\nSatsuki Ina\, author of The Poet an
 d the Silk Girl\nAbout the Film from the Defiant to the Last website:\n“
 Based on lies and wartime propaganda\, during WWII the U.S. government for
 cibly removed and incarcerated more than 125\,000 innocent Japanese Americ
 ans in ten American concentration camps\, solely because of their race.\n
 “At all the prison sites\, despite the mythology of quiet compliance\, J
 apanese Americans showed moral courage\, resisted\, and refused to accept 
 the government’s abuse. Defiant to the Last tells the story of the Tule 
 Lake Segregation Center where dissident Japanese Americans were demonized 
 and punished for speaking out against the false wartime incarceration.”\
 nRevolution Books is showing this film because the story of resistance to 
 the unjust treatment of the Japanese Americans in WW II resonates deeply w
 ith our own time\, when immigrants’ rights are stripped away\, they are 
 demonized\, and some deported to torture prisons in countries they’ve ne
 ver lived in – and people who oppose this treatment are attacked and vil
 ified by the government.\nThis is a time for defiance\, for voices of cons
 cience to speak out\, and for revolution. Defiant to the Last brings cruci
 al experience and important lessons from the past\, and we are very glad t
 o be able to bring Satsuki Ina and Emiko Omori to our store.\nWatch th...\
 n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://revolutionbooks.org\nDetails: https://sf.funch
 eap.com/film-defiant-resistance-tule-lake-jail/\nSource: Funcheap SF
