BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“The Stoner Comedy Jam” Friday Nights
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T213000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1639236@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Comedy Event Types Event
DESCRIPTION:“The Stoner Comedy Jam” Friday Nights (SF)\nHellaFunny\nYo
 u know what makes stand-up comedy funnier? Smoking while watching it live!
  Come to San Francisco’s premiere cannabis club Moe Greens every Friday 
 night for a night of laughter and\, well\, getting stoned.\nHellaFunny is 
 taking over the cannabis lounge at Moe Greens for the Stoner Comedy Jam. I
 t’s one of the only comedy show in San Francisco where you can (legally 
 in California) get high during the show.\n\nThe Stoner Comedy Jam\nEvery F
 riday at 8pm\nMoe Greens\, 1276 Market St.\, San Francisco\nFree with Gues
 t List RSVP\n\nIt’s a 70+ minute show with 4-5 of SF’s top local comic
 s on the bill\n21+ only\nOne item minimum purchase required\n\nFAQ\nIs thi
 s comedy show really free?\nYes! Just make sure to RSVP to get on the gues
 tlist. You must be 21+.\nTell me about the one-item minimum.\nIn order to 
 hook you up with this free comedy show\, there’s one-item minimum purcha
 se per person\, but it’s super affordable (and way cheaper than a tradit
 ional two-drink minimum at a bar!)\nDo I need a medical marijuana card?\nN
 ope! All you need to be is 21+ and have a valid ID.\nDo I have to smoke du
 ring the show?\nNope! You can smoke\, dab\, eat a gummy.. whatever you wan
 t! Or you can just enjoy the show. The one-item minimum purchase still app
 lies. So buy something and a give it to a friend! If you do decide to cons
 ume onsite\, just make sure to take is slow and know your body and your li
 mits.\nCan I bring outside weed?\nSorry! That’s not cool (and it’s not
  legal). In...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.universe.com/events/the-sf-
 stoner-comedy-jam-friday-nights-at-8p-tickets-8P0JBR\nDetails: https://sf.
 funcheap.com/the-stoner-comedy-jam-friday-nights-sf-191/\nSource: Funcheap
  SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/HalfBa
 ked_eventbrite.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Moe Greens\, 1276 Market St.\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/the-stoner-comedy-jam-friday-nights-sf-191/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aliens (Special Edition)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T204500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T224500
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17923121@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Where its predecessor was a slow-burn suspenser\, Cameron’s 
 ALIENS is a bombastic\, no-holds-barred exosuit fight to the finish\, an e
 xpress elevator to hell\, goin’ down! Lone survivor Ripley (Sigourney We
 aver) goes back for a rematch with the creatures who slaughtered the crew 
 of the Nostromo\, this time bringing along a squad of hard-boiled space ma
 rines whose number includes the great Bill Paxton\, Jenette Goldstein\, an
 d Lance Henriksen’s mumblety-peg-playing android Bishop. Rounding out th
 e superb supporting players are the aliens themselves\, pinnacles of pre-C
 GI visual effects that just keep coming\, and coming\, and coming\, and co
 ming… while Mead’s contributions can mostly be seen in the blade-like 
 military vessel Sulaco and the unforgettable “Power Loader” donned by 
 Ripley for the main event grudge match.\n\nScreening in Cameron’s prefer
 red cut\, which adds nearly 20 minutes of material not seen in the theatri
 cal version\, including glimpses of life at the ill-fated Hadley’s Hope 
 colony and some “kickass” motion-activated turret guns.\n\n“Hot off 
 of the immediate successes of Blade Runner and TRON\, Syd Mead was enliste
 d by Cameron to build out the world of ALIENS\, his muscular\, action-orie
 nted second chapter to Ridley Scott’s now-iconic 1979 masterpiece. The c
 enterpiece of Mead’s designs is the U.S.S. Sulaco\, the military spacesh
 ip that transports the Colonial Marines\, infusing the vessel with a funct
 ional and industrial aesthetic that enhanced the film’s gritty realism.
 ” —Future P...\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase
 /22258?siteToken=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: https://dothebay.com
 /events/2026/11/20/aliens-special-edition-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34800079/e4312bef-0067-4306-97a0-5d1d1f94d6db.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/20/aliens-special-edition-tickets
END:VEVENT
