BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Songs\, Sermons & Sacred Voyeurism
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTSTAMP:20261109T222818Z
UID:dothebay-18051610@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Variety
DESCRIPTION:Doors 7:30pm / Show 8pm\n\nFree | RSVP Optional\n\nA live acti
 vation in The Chapel of Becoming\, organized by Chani Bockwinkel in collab
 oration with Leila Weefur\n\nSongs\, Sermons & Sacred Voyeurism extends th
 e aesthetic and spiritual inquiry of The Chapel of Becoming into the body\
 , the voice\, and the act of witness. Part performance\, part ritual archi
 tecture\, the work draws on the long tradition of sacred song as a technol
 ogy of transformation\, and on the peep show as a structure of longing\, o
 bscured presence\, and controlled revelation.\n\nPerformers move through t
 he space using techniques of visual obstruction and partial disclosure\, m
 aking themselves available to be seen and not\, extending the exhibition's
  meditation on thresholds\, devotion\, and what it means to become. Simult
 aneously\, visitors are invited into sound experiences where vocal perform
 ances unfold in intimate isolation\, a format of auditory voyeurism where 
 listening borders on lustful and asks listeners to receive the voice as an
  act of devotion.\n\nTogether these modes\, the body in motion and the dis
 embodied voice\, produce a devotional space that refuses the separation of
  the sacred from the sensorial.\n\nFeaturing performances by Maxe Crandall
 \, Elya Piazza\, Snowflake Arizmendi-Calvert\, Alma Carmina Marquexz\, Sty
 les Alexander\, B Dean\, Hands\, and Mudd the Two Spirit\, with additional
  performers to be announced.\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/
 11/21/songs-sermons-sacred-voyeurism-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.765289;-122.418493
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35368036/36e238be-61a7-40fd-bd18-a767c0671711.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109T222818Z
LOCATION:The Lab\, 2948 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21/songs-sermons-sacred-voyeurism-
 tickets
END:VEVENT
