CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Bay Beats\, San Francisco Public Library's local music streami
 ng platform\, is throwing a rap showcase featuring three top Bay Beats rap
 pers. Witness their performances at the Main Library as they sharpen words
  into a celebratory wake-up call about life in the Bay and beyond. Full li
 ne-up:\n\n3 p.m. - Lil MC - a Latina powerhouse in the music industry\, Li
 L MC embodies the spirit of hip hop with her dynamic delivery\, sassy wit\
 , and bilingual flow. She has shared stages with legends like Jacquees\, T
 oo Short and E-40\, and is among the mere 3% of women music producers glob
 ally\, significantly contributing to the diversification of the music indu
 stry. Stream Lil MC's album\, Flex Maquina\, on Bay Beats to prep for the 
 show!\n\n2 p.m. - Family Not A Group - @familynotagroup__ - Consisting of 
 17 members\, FNG is a dynamic and diverse San Francisco-based artist colle
 ctive that encompasses the spirit of community\, love\, and creative expre
 ssion.\n\n1 p.m. - Philip Bank$ - @phildeeznuts\, an Oakland rapper who de
 livers keen insights and visceral descriptions about his hometown with swa
 gger and emotion. Even the hooks carry bars that hit harder than most emce
 e's verses.\n\nThis show is presented by Bay Beats\, in partnership with W
 hite Crate.\n\nFree\n\nPresented by San Francisco Public Library\n\nFree\n
 San Francisco Public Library\n\nTickets: https://on.sfpl.org/BayBeats-Rap\
 nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21/the-bay-beats-rap-show-ti
 ckets\nSource: DoTheBay
