DESCRIPTION:Brutalismus 3000 are the duo of producer Theo Zeitner and sing
 er Victoria Vassiliki Daldas\, two musical visionaries who met on Tinder i
 n 2018 and formed their antagonistic techno band in 2020. With an early hi
 t titled “Satan Was a Babyboomer” and fan-favorite lyrics about “fuc
 kface bouncers\,” Brutalismus 3000’s playful attitude and aggressive s
 ound were always too animated for Berlin’s restrictive techno scene. Eve
 n so\, after rising to fame online during COVID lockdown\, the band’s vi
 ral songs exploded in European clubs once live music returned\, resonating
  deeply with younger listeners who gleefully reject stodgy genre purism. S
 ince the release of their high-voltage 2023 debut\, ULTRAKUNST (LIVE FROM 
 EARTH)\, Brutalismus 3000 have been mainstays of the international festiva
 l circuit -- EDC\, Primavera Sound\, Coachella\, Ultra\, Lollapalooza\, an
 d more -- and now have friends\, fans\, and collaborators strewn all acros
 s the globe.\n\nFor their exhilarating sophomore album\, Harmony\, Brutali
 smus 3000 aimed to emphasize their cross-continental influences in a way t
 hey never have. The record is a genre-mangling triumph that assembles elem
 ents of dubstep\, trap\, punk\, nu-metal\, and techno into an eclectic rom
 p of wall-to-wall bangers that includes their most evolved and exciting mu
 sic yet. Never have Brutalismus 3000 sounded this singular\, this sophisti
 cated\, this outlandishly absorbing. Harmony consumed every spare minute o
 f the band’s lives for two straight years\, a strenuous process that in.
 ..\n\n16+\nGoldenvoice Presents\n\nTickets: https://shop.axs.com/?c=axs&e=
 30567424546970281\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/22/brutali
 smus-3000-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7879104;-122.4215079
