BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Indigenous Voices: Joey Clift and Terria Smith in conversation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T203000
DTSTAMP:20261111T063824Z
UID:dothebay-18029374@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Literature
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we close out our Native American Heritage Month ser
 ies\, welcoming Joey Clift and Terria Smith to share their latest works 
 — We've Been Here The Whole Time! and I Love You So Many.\n\nFree to att
 end — RSVP required to reserve your seat.\n\nSpeakers\nJoey Clift is a L
 os Angeles-based\, Peabody and 2x Emmy Award-nominated comedian\, writer\,
  director\, producer and enrolled member of the Cowlitz Indian Tribe.\nJoe
 y attended college to become a local TV weather person because as a kid he
  didn’t see any Native American comedians on television\, and that made 
 him believe he wasn’t allowed to work in comedy. Since then he has learn
 ed that this is not true – and his comedy style reflects that. Joey’s 
 work has been featured in The Washington Post\, Pitchfork\, NPR\, Dead Mea
 t\, Dropout and Comedy Central.\n\nTerria Smith is a tribal member of the 
 Torres Martinez Desert Cahuilla Indians and a proud original Californian. 
 She is the editor of News from Native California magazine and director of 
 the Berkeley Roundhouse\, Heyday’s California Indian publishing program.
  Smith is also the editor of the 2023 anthology Know We Are Here: Voices o
 f Native California Resistance. She received her undergraduate degree at C
 al Poly Humboldt (formerly Humboldt State University) and earned her maste
 r’s degree at the UC Berkeley Graduate School of Journalism. She lives o
 n her ancestral homelands in the Coachella Valley with her puppy Havana.\n
 \nFree\nTelegraph Hill Arts and Literature Presents\n\nTickets: https://te
 lhil.it/Joey-and-Terria\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/28/i
 ndigenous-voices-joey-clift-and-terria-smith-in-conversation-tickets\nSour
 ce: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/indigenous-voic
 es-joey-clift-terria-smith-conversation/
GEO:37.800823;-122.407824
