DESCRIPTION:Project Open HandProject Open Hand’s World AIDS Day Open Hou
 se\nTuesday\, December 1\n730 Polk Street\, San Francisco\n5 – 7 PM\nJoi
 n Project Open Hand and other HIV/AIDS agencies as we commemorate World AI
 DS Day\, connect with our neighbors\, and share resources and opportunitie
 s with the community.\nEvent Highlights:\n\nA word from Project Open Hand 
 CEO\, Paul Hepfer\nGuided tours of Project Open Hand’s kitchen\nOpportun
 ities to connect with team members from Project Open Hand team\, ALRP\, Ma
 itri\, PRC\, Shanti Project\, and more\nDelicious bites and refreshments\n
 Exclusive POH-branded swag for attendees\n\nWe’re proud to share our spa
 ce with community partners\, supporters\, and neighbors like you! Join us 
 in honoring the past and shaping the future.\nThis event is free and open 
 to all but space may be limited. Please register here to secure your spot.
 \n\nIf you have questions about this event\, email our team at events@open
 hand.org or visit www.openhand.org/events.\n\nWe look forward to seeing yo
 u!\nA note about parking: there are parking garages within walking distanc
 e of our building. Street parking may be available. Rideshare options are 
 recommended.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.openhand.org/events/2026-worl
 d-aids-day-open-house\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/world-aids-day-fre
 e-kitchen-tours-bites-project-open-hand/\nSource: Funcheap SF
