DESCRIPTION:Another Planet Entertainment presents\nA Janus Films and Crite
 rion Release\nCameron Winter at Carnegie Hall\nDirected by Paul Thomas And
 erson\nPresented in 35mm\n\nWednesday\, December 2 | The Castro\n\nCameron
  Winter\, in December 2025\, after a months-long sold-out tour with his ba
 nd Geese\, returned to New York to play a single show at Carnegie Hall. Th
 is is the movie.\n\nDirected and shot on 35mm and 16mm by Oscar-winning fi
 lmmaker Paul Thomas Anderson (One Battle After Another)\, the crew include
 s filmmaker and actor Benny Safdie (The Smashing Machine) and music produc
 er Ariel Rechtshaid (Grammy winner for albums with Vampire Weekend and Ade
 le).\n\nGQ praised Cameron Winter’s show at Carnegie Hall as “staggeri
 ngly good\,” and Nick Cave said he has a “a glorious\, emotive voice w
 ith brilliant\, blistering words\, a racked and wondrous thing.” Winter
 ’s solo album Heavy Metal was named one of the best of the year by Pitch
 fork\, Rolling Stone\, Paste and Mojo and Geese’s last record Getting Ki
 lled was named the best album of 2025 by The New Yorker\, NME\, and Stereo
 gum.\n\nAll Ages\nSold out\nAnother Planet Entertainment presents\nListed 
 time is doors\n\nTickets: https://thecastro.com/events/cameron-winter-at-c
 arnegie-hall-261202\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/2/camero
 n-winter-at-carnegie-hall-directed-by-paul-thomas-anderson-presented-in-35
 mm-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
