SUMMARY:Cameron Winter at Carnegie Hall
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T211500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T231500
DTSTAMP:20261109T222818Z
UID:dothebay-17963784@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Late Screening!Another Planet Entertainment presents\nA Janus 
 Films and Criterion Release\nCameron Winter at Carnegie Hall\nDirected by 
 Paul Thomas Anderson\nPresented in 35mm\n\nWednesday\, December 2 | The Ca
 stro\n\nCameron Winter\, in December 2025\, after a months-long sold-out t
 our with his band Geese\, returned to New York to play a single show at Ca
 rnegie Hall. This is the movie.\n\nDirected and shot on 35mm and 16mm by O
 scar-winning filmmaker Paul Thomas Anderson (One Battle After Another)\, t
 he crew includes filmmaker and actor Benny Safdie (The Smashing Machine) a
 nd music producer Ariel Rechtshaid (Grammy winner for albums with Vampire 
 Weekend and Adele).\n\nGQ praised Cameron Winter’s show at Carnegie Hall
  as “staggeringly good\,” and Nick Cave said he has a “a glorious\, 
 emotive voice with brilliant\, blistering words\, a racked and wondrous th
 ing.” Winter’s solo album Heavy Metal was named one of the best of the
  year by Pitchfork\, Rolling Stone\, Paste and Mojo and Geese’s last rec
 ord Getting Killed was named the best album of 2025 by The New Yorker\, NM
 E\, and Stereogum.\n\nAll Ages\nAnother Planet Entertainment presents: Lat
 e Screening!\nListed time is doors\n\nTickets: https://thecastro.com/event
 s/cameron-winter-at-carnegie-hall-261202-late\nDetails: https://dothebay.c
 om/events/2026/12/2/cameron-winter-at-carnegie-hall\nSource: DoTheBay
