DESCRIPTION:“Let’s Glow SF” 2026: SF’s Huge Holiday Projection Art
 s Festival (Dec. 4-13)\nDowntown San Francisco Partnership\nLet’s Glow S
 F\, the nation’s largest free holiday projection arts festival\, is ligh
 ting up downtown San Francisco once again for its sixth and brightest year
  yet.\nThis all-ages\, family-friendly festival runs for 10 dazzling night
 s from December 4-13\, 2026. Experience breathtaking animated projections 
 illuminating iconic buildings across downtown San Francisco\, transforming
  them into colossal\, colorful canvases featuring spectacular artwork by 1
 9 artists from around the globe. It’s a larger-than-life holiday light s
 how that turns the heart of the city into an open-air art gallery after da
 rk.\n\n2026 Let’s Glow SF Festival Showtimes\n\nFriday\, December 4: Cou
 ntdown to Glow opening-night celebration\, 6-7pm at Harry Bridges Plaza in
  front of the Ferry Building.\nFriday\, December 4: Festival projections\,
  7-10pm.\nDecember 5-13: Nightly projections\, 5:30-10pm.\n\n2026 Show Loc
 ations (map)\n\nFerry Building (1 Ferry Building) – Best viewed from Har
 ry Bridges Plaza.\n101 California St. (101 California St.) – Best viewed
  from inside 101 California Plaza.\nPacific Exchange (301 Pine St.) – Be
 st viewed from 300 Pine Street.\nHobart Building (582 Market St.) – Best
  viewed from 1 Post Street.\nYerba Buena Lane (Market St.) – Best viewed
  from Yerba Buena Lane off Market Street.\nSalesforce Tower (415 Mission S
 t.) – Best viewed from anywhere in downtown.\n\nLGSF Business Specials\n
 Participating down...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.downtownsf.org/event
 s/letsglowsf/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/lets-glow-sf/\nSource: Fun
 cheap SF
