BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SF’s Free Howard Zinn Book Fair: 40 Panels w/ Authors + Activist
 s (2026)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T180000
DTSTAMP:20261111T063824Z
UID:funcheap-1646700@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lgbtq
DESCRIPTION:Howard Zinn Book FairIf ever there was a time to create our ow
 n history rather than let malevolent people write it for us\, that time is
  now! Meet the people and groups helping build a world that serves everyon
 e at the Howard Zinn Book Fair\, Sunday\, December 6\, from 10am to 6pm\, 
 at the San Francisco City College Mission Campus\, 1125 Valencia Street. T
 his year’s theme is A Time of Monsters\, A Time to Fight.\n\nThe Howard 
 Zinn Book Fair started in 2014 as an annual celebration and this year feat
 ures 40 panel discussions by authors and activists and a big room full of 
 independent presses\, community groups\, artists\, and non-profits. All of
  our participants focus on empowering people to become engaged in the stru
 ggle for a truly participatory and democratic society.\n\nWe live in a tim
 e when many are asked to survive what can only be called monstrous: author
 itarianism\, war\, state violence\, environmental destruction\, economic i
 nsecurity\, forced displacement\, attacks on civil rights\, and the everyd
 ay cruelties of systems built to dehumanize. But throughout history\, ordi
 nary people have resisted monstrous situations and individuals in order to
  take more control of their future.\n\nThis year we have dozens of speaker
 s including renowned journalist Dave Zirin\, whose new book The People’s
  Historian: The Outsized Life of Howard Zinn is a groundbreaking profile o
 f our book fair’s namesake\, the radical historian and thought leader Ho
 ward Zinn.\n\nOther speakers include Rachel Herzing\, Jordan Camp\,...\n\n
 Free\n\nTickets: https://www.zinnbookfair.org/\nDetails: https://sf.funche
 ap.com/sfs-free-howard-zinn-book-fair-40-panels-authors-activists-2026/\nS
 ource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Howard
 -Zinn-image-from-website-Nov_26.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111T063824Z
LOCATION:City College of SF (Mission Campus)\, 1125 Valencia St.\, San Fra
 ncisco\, CA 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-free-howard-zinn-book-fair-40-panels-autho
 rs-activists-2026/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:East Bay Open Studios
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T170000
DTSTAMP:20261112T112617Z
UID:caldiscovery-festival-7e2da86489bb2313@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:arts,community,festival,free
DESCRIPTION:Category: Art / Photography / Crafts\,Community Events / Volun
 teerism\,Festivals / ParadesContact Phone: 510-842-6876Contact Email: ebos
 @oaklandartmurmur.orgCost: FreeLink: https://www.eastbayopenstudios.comEas
 t Bay Open Studios returns for two free weekends with over 180 artists ope
 ning their studios to the public. This free\, self-guided event invites yo
 u to wander into local studios\, galleries\, and community hubs in Oakland
 \, Berkeley\, and beyond. Come curious — meet the creative minds behind 
 the work\, experience art where it's made\, and leave inspired.Not sure wh
 ere to start? Explore our Emerging Artists\, Community Hubs\, or find your
  favorite artwork using our Artist Directory!🗓️ Open Studios: Dec 5-6
  and 12-13\; 11am–5pm daily 📍 Art in your neighborhoods across the Ea
 st Bay🎫 Get your free ticket: EventbriteHOW TO PARTICIPATE:1. Visit eas
 tbayopenstudios.com2. Browse artist profiles or use the interactive maps (
 Weekend 1 + Weekend 2)3. Don't know where to start? Check out our Emerging
