DESCRIPTION:Cameron Winter\, in December 2025\, after a months-long sold-o
 ut tour with his band Geese\, returned to New York to play a single show a
 t Carnegie Hall. This is the movie.\n\nDirected and shot on 35mm and 16mm 
 by Oscar-winning filmmaker Paul Thomas Anderson (One Battle After Another)
 \, the crew includes filmmaker and actor Benny Safdie (The Smashing Machin
 e) and music producer Ariel Rechtshaid (Grammy winner for albums with Vamp
 ire Weekend and Adele).\n\nGQ praised Cameron Winter’s show at Carnegie 
 Hall as “staggeringly good\,” and Nick Cave said he has a “a gloriou
 s\, emotive voice with brilliant\, blistering words\, a racked and wondrou
 s thing.” Winter’s solo album Heavy Metal was named one of the best of
  the year by Pitchfork\, Rolling Stone\, Paste and Mojo and Geese’s last
  record Getting Killed was named the best album of 2025 by The New Yorker\
 , NME\, and Stereogum.\n\nTickets for Saturday\, December 5 at 4 PM availa
 ble here\n\nTickets for Sunday\, December 6 at 1 PM available here\n\nMore
  showtimes will be added.\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 15m\n\nYear\n\n2026\n\nDirector
