DESCRIPTION:UsThree Rooms Press presents\nThe 13th Annual\nSF ¡DADA! DO S
 ALON\n\nA Highly Eclectic DADA Performance Event\nplus the official San Fr
 ancisco launch of\nMAINTENANT 20: Journal of Contemporary DADA Writing and
  Art\n\nSunday\, December 6\, 2026 | 6 pm PST\nSPEC’S Twelve Adler Museu
 m Cafe\n12 William Saroyan Place\, North Beach\, San Francisco\nFree Admis
 sion\n\nAn evening of provocative\, exuberant\, eclectic performance and p
 oetry is slated to hit the stage as Three Rooms Press presents 2026 SF ¡D
 ADA! DO SALON: a wild ride of contemporary DADA performance and poetry by 
 leading Bay Area maverick artists The event includes the official San Fran
 cisco launch of the internationally-renowned MAINTENANT 20: Journal of Con
 temporary Dada Writing and Art (2026\, Three Rooms Press)\, which features
  more than 230 visual and literary works by artists and writers from six c
 ontinents.\n\nThe event takes place Sunday\, December 6\, 6 pm\, at SPECS
 ’ Twelve Adler Museum Cafe\, 12 William Saroyan Place in North Beach. Ad
 mission is free. Costumes encouraged. Come as you aren’t.\n\nThe line-up
  features renowned contemporary DADA artists from the Bay Area and beyond 
 including Mahnaz Badihian\, Allison A. Davis\, Carol Dorf\, Jon Longhi\, R
 ichard Loranger\, Robyn Mallery\, Thomas Stolmar\, Rich Stone\, Tate Swind
 ell\, Maw Shein Win\, and Lorene Zarou-Zouzounis. Three Rooms Press co-fou
 nders and MAINTENANT editors Peter Carlaftes and Kat Georges host.\n\nPlus
  after the reading\, for an added attraction\, pianist/singer Wendy Fitz a
 nd bassist...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://threeroomspress.com/event/13th-a
 nnual-sf-dada-do-salon/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/13th-annual-sf-d
