DESCRIPTION:Foodwise Presents\nPop-Ups on the Plaza: Black Holiday Market\
 n\nSaturday\, December 12 (9am-2pm) | Ferry Plaza Farmers Market\n\nCelebr
 ate local Black-owned businesses and get ready for the holiday season with
  a day of delicious food\, crafts\, and community at the Ferry Plaza Farme
 rs Market. The south arcade of the Ferry Building will be transformed for 
 a special holiday market featuring 20 Bay Area food makers and designers. 
 Find thoughtful gifts and stocking stuffers for everyone on your list\, li
 ke food crafts\, skincare\, apparel\, gift cards\, and more. Entry is free
  and open to the public\, with products available for purchase.\n\nPop-Ups
  on the Plaza is a series of events celebrating Bay Area BIPOC entrepreneu
 rs\, including businesses in Foodwise’s Building Equity program. Pop-Ups
  on the Plaza is a Port sponsored event brought to you by Foodwise. This p
 rogram is proudly funded in partnership with the San Francisco Human Right
 s Commission. Additional support is provided by the Ferry Building.\n\nPar
 ticipating Vendors\nA Girl Named Pinky: Cookies\, mini cakes\, cupcakes\, 
 cake pops\, and brownies\nAvocurl: Natural haircare products\nBelle Noire:
  Handcrafted accessories made by artists from Africa and the African Diasp
 ora\nBismillah Boutique: Handmade crystal-embellished candles and skincare
 \nBruthas Honey: Raw honey\, honeycomb\, and honey sticks\nCali Sweet Cake
 s: Mini bundt cakes and cookies\nChef Sarah Germany: Hot sauce and pickles
 \nCIK Apparel: Apparel and accessories\nCocoacentric: Stylish statem...\n\
 nFree\nFoodwise Presents\n\nTickets: https://foodwise.org/events/pop-ups-o
 n-the-plaza-black-holiday-market/\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/20
 26/12/12/pop-ups-on-the-plaza-black-holiday-market-tickets\nSource: DoTheB
 ay
