BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Little Women (2019)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T170000
DTSTAMP:20261023T171442Z
UID:dothebay-17979564@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Having already once revolutionized the coming-of-age story wit
 h her debut LADY BIRD\, Greta Gerwig has somehow outdone herself with this
  gorgeous and thoroughly original rendition of the beloved Louisa May Alco
 tt classic. Bringing her effusive humor\, authenticity\, and irresistible 
 warmth to the otherwise mannered Civil War-era New England\, Gerwig's adap
 tation of LITTLE WOMEN breathes visceral new life into the March sisters 
 – portraying them as unique\, complicated\, flawed\, and astonishingly h
 uman. So human that you will leave the theater wanting to text Jo March an
 d\, for several reasons\, this will not be a possibility.\n\nYou may also 
 find it physically impossible not to chef's kiss at the cast\, which is as
  close to pitch-perfect as it gets. Starring Saoirse Ronan as Jo\, Emma Wa
 tson as Meg\, Florence Pugh as Amy\, and Eliza Scanlen as Beth\, LITTLE WO
 MEN also features Laura Dern (!)\, Meryl Streep (!)\, Bob Odenkirk (!)\, a
 nd Timothée Chalamet as the dashing but lovelorn Laurie (!!!).\n\nSave fo
 r a fireworks show\, sky-written ode\, or Mount Rushmore-type situation\, 
 we cannot recommend this rich\, heartrending wonder of a film anymore. Its
  timeless charm is sure to capture the hearts of little women (and men) ev
 erywhere.\n\nTickets: https://drafthouse.com/sf/show/sad-girl-cinema-club-
 little-women-2019?cinemaId=0802&sessionId=23201\nDetails: https://dothebay
 .com/events/2026/12/13/little-women-2019-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7562198;-122.419185
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35067886/6be86249-5b6a-4751-8876-b2cc7ce2b4ed.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T171442Z
LOCATION:Alamo Drafthouse Cinema\, 2550 Mission St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/13/little-women-2019-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Let’s Glow SF” 2026: SF’s Huge Holiday Projection Arts Fe
 stival (Final Night)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T220000
DTSTAMP:20261104T012711Z
UID:funcheap-1645857@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art Museums
DESCRIPTION:“Let’s Glow SF” 2026: SF’s Huge Holiday Projection Art
 s Festival (Dec. 4-13)\nDowntown San Francisco Partnership\nLet’s Glow S
 F\, the nation’s largest free holiday projection arts festival\, is ligh
 ting up downtown San Francisco once again for its sixth and brightest year
  yet.\nThis all-ages\, family-friendly festival runs for 10 dazzling night
 s from December 4-13\, 2026. Experience breathtaking animated projections 
 illuminating iconic buildings across downtown San Francisco\, transforming
  them into colossal\, colorful canvases featuring spectacular artwork by 1
 9 artists from around the globe. It’s a larger-than-life holiday light s
 how that turns the heart of the city into an open-air art gallery after da
 rk.\n\n2026 Let’s Glow SF Festival Showtimes\n\nFriday\, December 4: Cou
 ntdown to Glow opening-night celebration\, 6-7pm at Harry Bridges Plaza in
  front of the Ferry Building.\nFriday\, December 4: Festival projections\,
  7-10pm.\nDecember 5-13: Nightly projections\, 5:30-10pm.\n\n2026 Show Loc
 ations (map)\n\nFerry Building (1 Ferry Building) – Best viewed from Har
 ry Bridges Plaza.\n101 California St. (101 California St.) – Best viewed
  from inside 101 California Plaza.\nPacific Exchange (301 Pine St.) – Be
 st viewed from 300 Pine Street.\nHobart Building (582 Market St.) – Best
  viewed from 1 Post Street.\nYerba Buena Lane (Market St.) – Best viewed
  from Yerba Buena Lane off Market Street.\nSalesforce Tower (415 Mission S
 t.) – Best viewed from anywhere in downtown.\n\nLGSF Business Specials\n
 Participating down...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.downtownsf.org/event
 s/letsglowsf/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/lets-glow-sf-2026-sfs-huge
 -holiday-projection-arts-festival-final-night/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Lets-G
 low-SF.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T012711Z
LOCATION:San Francisco’s Financial District\, Market at Sutter Street\, 
 San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/lets-glow-sf-2026-sfs-huge-holiday-projection-
 arts-festival-final-night/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yaelokre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T200000
DTSTAMP:20261014T214646Z
UID:dothebay-17493380@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Another Planet Entertainment presents\nYaelokre\n\nSunday\, De
 cember 13 | The Castro\n\nIf you ever feel as if music has lost its capaci
 ty for surprise\, the beguiling wonder and infinite creativity of Yaelokre
  will respark your belief. The Filipino-Icelandic artist – real name Kea
 th Ósk (they/it) – fuses three imaginative strands to their visionary e
 xpression: intimate\, innocent folk infused with leftfield surrealism and 
 instant pop accessibility\; artwork which is intricately detailed and beau
 tifully alluring\; and storytelling which brings personal experience and p
 oetry into rich\, fable-like narratives. What’s more\, all three of thes
 e elements are crafted by this one visionary artist.\n\nThe scale of the f
 antastical world they have created is vast\, both in terms of narrative an
 d lore. But its essence is relatively simple. The songs are set in the fic
 tional world of Meadowlark and chart the adventures of four masked childre
 n who comprise a musical ensemble known at The Lark: Cole Seymour\, Cléme
 nte Dearworth\, Peregrine August\, and Kingsley. They perform as represent
 atives of The Harkers\, mythical beings who express the fundamental princi
 ples of nature\, wonder and chaos. What’s more\, Yaelokre voices all of 
 the different characters within their universe.\n\nThis immersive\, escapi
 st story is largely inspired by Yaelokre’s own life. The four Larks repr
 esent different stages of their childhood\, and writing their songs felt c
 athartic for their creator. As Yaelokre explains\, “Their stories are...
 \n\nall ages\nAnother Planet Entertainment presents\nListed time is doors\
 n\nTickets: https://ticketmaster.evyy.net/c/253185/264167/4272?SharedId=Do
 Stuff&u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ticketmaster.com%2Fyaelokre-san-francisco-califo
 rnia-12-13-2026%2Fevent%2F1C0064CF8D5A6CA1%3Fcamefrom%3DCFC_ANOTHERPLANET_
 web%26brand%3Danotherplanet\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/
 13/yaelokre-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7619917;-122.4347365
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/32770740/d8d18276-905a-45f0-89fb-42d25a9a69a0.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261014T214646Z
LOCATION:The Castro\, 429 Castro St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94114
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/13/yaelokre-tickets
END:VEVENT
