BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:3rd Annual A Very Purple NYE! With Purple Rain And Sign "O" The Ti
 mes!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261231T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261231T230000
DTSTAMP:20261101T160546Z
UID:dothebay-17865876@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:The VOGUE Theatre Presents ~\n\nA Very Purple New Years Eve!\n
 3rd Annual NYE Party!\n\nFeaturing A 4K Restoration Of\nPURPLE RAIN\nAnd\n
 Concert Film ~ Sign ☮️ The Times\n\nThursday December 31 New Years Eve
 !\nDoors Open At 9:00pm\nPurple Music Videos\, Before The Film!\nPurple Ra
 in Starting At 10:00pm\n\nMidnight Countdown With Complimentary Champagne 
 Toast* And Party Favors!\n\nThen Right Into Sign ☮️ The Times\,\nKeepi
 ng The Party Going!\n\nTickets Are Just $25- And All Ages Welcome!\n\nPurp
 le Rain ~\n"The Kid" (Prince) is a troubled Minneapolis musician. He and h
 is band\, The Revolution are one of three acts playing at a local nightclu
 b\, the First Avenue. The other acts are The Time\, a funk band\, lead by 
 Morris Day and The Modernaires\, a new wave band\, lead by Dez Dickerson.\
 nAspiring singer Apollonia\, comes to town to try her luck hoping to get h
 ired as singer at the First Avenue. Both "The Kid" and Morris Day are attr
 acted to her and vie for her attention. While a romance starts to develop 
 between "The Kid" and Apollonia\, she accepts a position in Morris Day’s
  new all female group\, Apollonia 6\, to the obvious dismay of "The Kid". 
 Will The Kid take the top spot?\n\nSign ☮️ The Times ~\nMusic legend P
 rince and his band perform 13 numbers\, most of them from his double album
 \, "Sign 'o' the Times." This is high-energy stuff: neon signs flash above
  the stage\, suggesting the honky-tonk district of a big city\, and betwee
 n numbers there are vignettes of street life. Sheila E.\, Boni Boyer and C
 at provide rhyth...\n\n$25-\nVogue Theater\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.u
 swest.veezi.com/purchase/19859?siteToken=qkwymq4me4nthdzzgj9fe08j0r\nDetai
